# Normalise to LF in the repository for everything textual.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Golden vectors are byte-compared: CI regenerates them and fails on any diff
# (see .github/workflows/ci.yml). The generator writes LF, so a checkout that
# converted these to CRLF would report drift that does not exist and fail the
# build on Windows only. Disable conversion outright rather than relying on the
# eol=lf above, because these files are artifacts, not source.
testdata/vectors/*.json -text

# Same reasoning, for the scenario recordings that land with vigil-sim.
testdata/scenarios/** -text

# Same reasoning again: the export-pack fixtures (binary) and the expected-verdict
# JSON that vigil-verify is cross-checked against are CI-regenerated and byte-compared.
testdata/packs/** -text
